<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica Cosatu to march for &quot;people's budget&quot;.</title>
<headline>SAfrica Cosatu to march for &quot;people's budget&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's largest labour group Cosatu said on Tuesday it planned to march on parliament on budget day to call for a &quot;people's budget&quot;.</p>
<p>The union said the March 12 demonstration would ask Finance Minister Trevor Manuel to increase spending on education, health, welfare, public works and water.</p>
<p>The ruling African National Congress is in an uneasy alliance with Cosatu and the South African Communist Party, and its market-friendly policies have angered some in the labour movement.</p>
<p>Last week Cosatu said it would begin mobilising its members for a general strike on May 12 over a planned employment bill.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
